erview": "Iowa's open Senate seat is one of the closest races of 2026. Joni Ernst's retirement leaves Republicans with Ashley Hinson, a well-funded congresswoman, against Democrat Josh Turek, a veteran and former Paralympian. Both sides have poured in outside money, including a $20 million Senate Leadership Fund commitment for Hinson.\n\nPolling is genuinely mixed: independent pollsters like the New York Times/Siena and Fox News show a dead heat, while some Republican-leaning firms put Hinson ahead and others show Turek up. Averages give Turek a one-to-two-point edge, but prediction markets lean slightly toward Hinson. Nearly every expert rater calls it a tossup, with only Inside Elections tilting Republican. The race sits right on the knife's edge heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.503, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.579, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5896, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5557, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.499, "margin": -0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5985, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.607, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.6056, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.506, "margin": 0.5}]}